\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus, Thou soul of all our joys,
\par For whom we now lift up our voice
\par And all our strength exert,
\par Vouchsafe the grace we humbly
\par claim,
\par Compose into a thankful frame,
\par And tune Thy people's heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. While in the heavenly work we
\par join,
\par Thy glory be our whole design,
\par Thy glory, not our own:
\par Still let us keep our end in view,
\par And still the pleasing task pursue,
\par To please our God alone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The secret pride, the subtle sin,
\par O let it never more steal in,
\par To offend Thy glorious eyes,
\par To desecrate our hallowed strain,
\par And make our solemn service vain,
\par And mar our sacrifice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. With calmly reverential joy,
\par O let us all our lives employ
\par In setting forth Thy love;
\par And raise in death our triumph
\par higher,
\par And sing with all the heavenly choir
\par That endless song above!
\par                            Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

